The fill that turns tracing on leaves the turn owing from where it was in the tick.
Under tracing the clock is the tick count, so QEMU would charge the first traced tick less than the host;
a traced turn is charged from the tick.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a traced turn is charged from within a tick

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -367,7 +367,6 @@ void sched_accounts_fill(void)
     /* The fill clears what every core's turn owed, too. */
     for (uint32_t c = 0; c < CORES; c++) {
         LOOP_BOUND(CORES);
-        cores[c].turn_from = clock_offset();
         cores[c].nearest_release = sched_ticks + NEAREST_NONE;
     }
     for (uint32_t i = 0; i < MACHINE_UNITS; i++) {
